# Hero Line Wars

WC3-style **hero line wars** (not a MOBA). 2D top-down Canvas, wave line, sends, shop, relics, Artifacts (turrets). Prefer modular files; ship playable loops before new systems.

## Stack & deploy

- **Vite + TypeScript**, Canvas 2D world, light DOM for menus/HUD. No React.
- Targets: `build:pages` → `dist/`; `build:release` → single-file HTML; `desktop:dist` → Electron (`DESKTOP.md`). Thin Electron shell over the same Vite build.
- Pages: `.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml` builds + deploys `dist/` on `master` (repo Settings → Pages → Source: GitHub Actions).
- Art generators: `tools/generate-*-art.mjs` → `public/art/{relics,items}/`.
- **Version + patch notes (required on meaningful change sets):** main menu shows `package.json` `version` (Vite `define` → `__APP_VERSION__`). Same approach as LaneBreakers — do this in the **same pass** as the feature/fix work, not as an optional follow-up.
  - **One bump per uncommitted change set.** If `package.json` version is still what HEAD (last commit) has, bump it once (patch semver: `0.0.N` → `0.0.N+1`) and open **one** new `PATCHNOTES.md` section headed with today’s date + that version (newest first).
  - **Do not bump again** for later prompts in the same uncommitted batch. Append bullets under the **existing** top section for that version. A brand-new version section each chat/prompt is wrong and over-fragments the changelog.
  - Only start a **new** version section when the previous bumped version is already committed (or the user explicitly asks for a fresh release cut).
  - Every player-facing / agent-facing behavior change gets a concise bullet in that section. Update this rule and `README.md` when conventions or advertised features change.
  - Subagents / multitask workers must include version + patch notes in their deliverable when they touch gameplay or ship surface — omitting them is incomplete work.

## Where to change what

| Concern | Prefer |
|---|---|
| Heroes / abilities / passives | `src/data/heroes.ts` (+ combat in `systems/abilities.ts`, `systems/combat.ts`) |
| Shop gear & Artifacts | `src/data/shop.ts`, `src/data/turrets.ts`; apply in `systems/shop.ts`, `systems/turrets.ts` |
| Relics | `src/data/relics.ts` + `systems/relics.ts` |
| Sends / wave economy | `src/data/send.ts` + `systems/send.ts` |
| Maps / geometry / specials | `src/data/maps.ts` (flags + zone arrays on `MapDef`); runtime in `Game` / `render` / enemy pathing |
| Enemies | `src/data/enemies.ts` + `systems/enemies.ts` |
| XP / level drafts / hero perks | `src/data/xp.ts` + `systems/xp.ts` (hero-specific passives live with level drafts) |
| Base upgrades / branches | `src/data/baseUpgrades.ts`, `baseBranches.ts` + `systems/baseUpgrade.ts` |
| Meta (crests, barracks, challenges, ascension, locks) | `src/meta/*` especially `contentLocks.ts`, `challenges.ts`, `upgrades.ts` |
| Menus / settings / HUD chrome | `src/ui/*` (`MenuController.ts`, `mainMenuFx.ts`, `style.css`, …) |
| Net / lobby / MP | `src/net/*` (`types.ts`, `lobby.ts`, `MultiplayerUi.ts`, `session.ts`, `mpSim.ts`, `sync.ts`, `playerBag.ts`) |
| Custom / editor content | `src/custom/*` (always sanitize via `validate.ts` on receive/save) |
| AI Lab | `src/ai/*` |

Match existing patterns; don't invent parallel systems or one-off globals.

## Content authoring

- Stable **snake_case ids**; add to the typed union + def table in the same change.
- Unlocks: challenges → barracks / War Crests via `meta/contentLocks.ts` + `challenges.ts` — don't hard-gate only in UI.
- New maps: fill `MapDef` geometry **and** any specials (`shiftingObstacles`, `shrinkingLane`, `healSprings`, `windCurrents`, `emberRain`, `supplyDrops`, `chronoPulse`, …). Wire flags must already be handled in game/render or extend those call sites — data alone is not enough.
- Player-facing name **Artifact**; internal code may still say turret.
- After new relics/items, regenerate SVG art scripts when icons are expected. Hero portraits are not used currently.
- Hero level perks: add to `LEVEL_PASSIVES` (or hero-gated entries) with rarity; Compendium **Bonuses** tab reads the same list — keep SP drafts and Compendium in sync.

## Shared policy helpers (use these — don't re-derive)

| Question | Helper |
|---|---|
| How many humans are in this game? | `humanPlayerCount(target)` — `src/game/pause.ts` |
| May anything pause the sim? | `canPauseSimulation(target)`; drafts use `canPauseForDraft`, future aim-freeze uses `canFreezeForAim` |
| Are gameplay cheats live? | `gameplayCheats(state)` / `gameplayCheatsAllowed(state)` — `src/meta/cheats.ts` (never call `areCheatsEnabled()` for gameplay effects) |
| What does this wave contain? | `planWaveSpawns` → `beginWaveFromPlan` / `spawnWaveSpecials` / `prepareLaneGeometryForWave` — `src/systems/waves.ts` |
| Give the player a reward draft | `openOrQueueDraft(state, draft)`; after resolving one call `syncDraftFlags(state)` — `src/systems/drafts.ts` |
| Is a remote intent safe? | `sanitizeIntent(raw)` + `IntentRateLimiter` — `src/net/intentGuard.ts` |

Rules that follow from them:

- **Pause is decided by human head-count only**, never by "is this mpSim". `GameState.humanPlayers` is stamped by `setMatchHumanPlayers` (`matchFactory`) and carried in `LaneSnap`. One human (incl. offline solo team / neural / AI Lab) may pause; two or more may not, anywhere.
- **Cheats mirror the same rule.** Gameplay cheats are off with >1 human, host included. `unlockAll` stays allowed.
- **Never assign `relicDraft` / `levelDraft` / `chestDraft` / `pausedForDraft` directly** — go through the draft queue so a second reward is queued rather than clobbered, and so the queue rides along in the bag snapshot.
- New creative/run flags that change wave content belong in `planWaveSpawns`, not in either `startWave`.

## SP / MP run-option parity

Creative and run extras must stay in sync across:

- `LobbyState` / `MpRunExtras` in `src/net/types.ts`
- Solo run options UI in `MenuController`
- Host lobby sync in `MultiplayerUi` (+ match start / `matchFactory`)

Adding a toggle in SP only (or MP only) is a bug. Mirror fields, defaults, and apply paths.

Fog UI fields: `sp-fog-thickness` / `sp-fog-vision` (and MP equivalents). Run fog, curse fog, and map eclipse fog **stack**: strongest opacity + tightest vision wins — don't replace one source with another.

## Multiplayer authority & independence (critical)

Shared **physical** lane (enemies, base HP, map, lane curses / hex zones). Independent **progression** per controller:

- Gold, shop open/stock/owned, relics, XP/level drafts, utility draft, curse/chest drafts that belong to the picker, rerolls — live in `playerBags` (`src/net/playerBag.ts`), swapped onto lane fields via `withPlayerBag` when applying that seat's intents.
- **Do not** gate shop / nearShop on the lane primary only — use the acting hero.
- **Do not** apply every seat's UI intents against one shared gold pool.
- Draft UI on clients **must** queue choices into `CombatIntent` (`chooseRelic`, `chooseLevel`, `chooseUtility`, `chooseCurse`, `chooseChest`, `chooseBaseBranch`, `skipRelic`, `rerollLevel`, `rerollRelic`) — never call `choose*` only on local state in MP.
- `LaneSnap` / `applyLaneSnap` must carry every draft kind clients need (utility, curse, chest, base branch, bags) or clients softlock.
- **Lane payloads are per-peer.** `buildMatchSnapFor(match, slot, viewTeam)` sends a full `LaneSnap` for the peer's own lane and the lane it is viewing, and a `LaneSummary` (wave, base, enemy count, players) for the rest. Clients announce a lane change with the `view` message; the host answers with an immediate full snapshot. Anything a client must **render or click** has to be in `LaneSnap` — audit `render/draw.ts` when adding world state. Fragile sync surfaces: fog, `mapSupplyCrates`, `laneGeometry` left/right — keep them on the snap path.
- Host binds intents to connection `fromSlot` — **ignore** client-claimed `seat` on intent messages.
- `viewTeam` / camera flip is **local-only** — never overwrite from host `MatchSnap` on clients.
- Entering a match must **not** call `disconnectNet()` — tear down lobby UI with `MultiplayerUi.destroy({ disconnect: false })` and clear lobby `bindHooks(null)`; keep PeerJS until `endMultiplayer` / leave.
- Shop vs send digit conflict: resolve against **local player's** shop-open bag, not the viewed opponent lane.
- Cross-lane sends: capture outbound in `stepMpMatch` buffers (do not leave a stub that never moves packs).
- Incoming `pendingSends` stay on the **lane** (not per-bag) so bag swaps cannot wipe them.

## SP vs MP sim parity

`src/net/mpSim.ts` must keep parity with `update()` in `game/state.ts` for:

- Curse timer ticks (shop / send / upgrade block, income tax, fog, shop refresh slow)
- Income tax applied to gold gain
- `hexZones` DoT
- AI allies (`controllerSlot < 0` or null): scripted/neural intents — never frozen statues

When adding a lane tick to SP, mirror it in `updateLaneMp` (or extract a shared helper).

## Maps & workshop (fragile)

- Playable **shapes** (`rect`, circle, polygon families) live on custom map defs; shape change uses `menu-confirm-overlay` and may clamp/drop placed objects — don't bypass the confirm path.
- Playable-edge hit-test and `playBounds` drive editor resize + in-match clamp — keep game/editor math aligned.
- Reuse workshop chrome: `workshop-*`, `run-field` / `run-grid`, `setting-row`, `muted-box`, `special-tag`.
- Mazing is classified Special (dual spawners) by design; Hex Bowl + Capsule Coast are the normal-shaped built-ins from that pass.

## Tests

`npm test` (Vitest, `tests/`) — `npm run typecheck` type-checks `src` + `tests`.
Cover new shared rules here: `tests/parity.test.ts` is a seeded SP-vs-dual-lane
harness, plus focused suites for pause policy, cheat gating, the draft queue,
run-option flags, custom-map sanitizing, save import and intent clamping. Browser
APIs are stubbed in `tests/setup.ts`; keep new logic importable without a DOM.

## Custom content safety

- Sanitize/clamp all peer and import payloads (`custom/validate.ts`): finite coords, array size caps, absurd stat clamps, ability/passive id checks.
- Settings: `rejectPeerCustoms` — when on, refuse MP starts that require custom maps/heroes so payloads are never registered for that match.
- Session customs are match-scoped (`registerSessionCustoms`); do not auto-write peer defs into the local library unless the player explicitly imports/saves.

## UI / UX design philosophy (shared layout system — prescriptive)

Menus are a **lane-wars war room**, not a generic dashboard and not a phone list. Preserve the **dark steel / amber-teal** identity. Never purple-on-white, cream-serif-terracotta, or broadsheet chrome. Fonts stay Orbitron / Rajdhani on brand surfaces.

### Tokens (use these, never hardcode replacements)

`--hlw-*` in `src/style.css`: `--hlw-bg`, `--hlw-panel`, `--hlw-border`, `--hlw-label`, `--hlw-text`, `--hlw-amber`, `--hlw-teal`, `--hlw-danger`, `--hlw-radius`, `--hlw-radius-lg`, shell widths `--hlw-shell-sm|md|lg|xl` (grow at ≥1920 / ≥2560 / ≥3840). New chrome derives from these tokens; per-screen hex constants are a review flag.

### Scroll policy (hard rule)

**Every menu screen must fit 1366×768 with no shell scrollbar** in its default state. The only permitted scroll surfaces:

- Compendium card list (unbounded content)
- Career Stats tab body
- Barracks / Challenges card grids (unbounded content)
- Patch Notes version body (one version per page; pager stays fixed)
- An **open** `details.opt-fold` (user opted in)
- Workshop side panel as a safety overflow only — its default content must fit

If a screen grows past the budget: group into columns, fold advanced options into `details.opt-fold`, or shorten copy. **Never** fix overflow by shrinking fonts below 0.7rem or letting a fixed overlay hide controls. Density trims for short viewports live in the `@media (max-height: 840px)` block — spacing only, not font size.

### Layout system — which shell/component for what

| Surface | Use |
|---|---|
| Screen chrome | `menu-shell` + modifier: `prefs-shell` (Settings/Controls/Cheats/AI Lab/Compendium/Patch Notes), `meta-shell` + `meta-hub` (Barracks/Challenges), `stats-shell`, `info-shell`, `workshop-shell` + `workshop-layout` (editors), `mp-shell`, `tight` (SP setup, editors) |
| Main menu | `main-menu-grid` with grouped `main-group` sections (Play / Progress / Workshop / Library / system row) — never one flat button column |
| Patch Notes | `prefs-layout patch-layout` · version pager (← newer / → older) · scrollable `.patch-body` sourced from root `PATCHNOTES.md` via `src/data/patchNotes.ts` |
| Run setup (SP + MP) | `sp-run-layout` (setup left, hero picker right) · `panel-head` (title + Reset/Randomize actions) · **one** dense `run-grid cols-3/cols-4` for core fields · `map-preview` (shape-aware canvas via `src/ui/mapThumbs.ts`) · creative options in `details.opt-fold` (collapsed unless non-default; summary shows `opt-count`) |
| Settings | `settings-groups` → 3 `settings-group` cards (Audio / Gameplay / Display & motion), `setting-row` rows |
| Controls | `bind-sections` → `bind-section` cards (Gamepad / Combat / Movement / Utility) |
| Editors | tools in a `workshop-toolbar` **above the canvas** inside `workshop-main`; identity + specials (`me-specials-grid`) + actions in `workshop-side`; template picker + library in `workshop-footer-bar` spanning both columns. The side panel must not scroll by default. |
| Form fields | `run-grid` + `run-field` (cols-2/3/4), `setting-row`, `creative-check-grid`, `cheats-toggle-grid`, `ai-lab-layout`, `meta-card-grid`, `hero-grid compact` (auto-fill minmax) |
| Advanced/optional groups | `details.opt-fold` (+ `.opt-fold-body`, `opt-count`); long-form help in `details.help-fold` |
| Confirmations | `menu-confirm-overlay` rendered from screen `render()` state (see softlock note below), never `window.confirm` |

Layout rules:

- Kill single-column node stacks wherever ≥2 columns fit. Grids use `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(…))` or explicit `cols-N` with media fallbacks — never fixed pixel columns.
- Modals/overlays must be produced by the screen's normal `render()` output so a re-render tears them down. **Never** append an overlay to the menu root outside the shell (this caused the map-editor shape-confirm softlock).
- Dark styled inputs only — never bare native light controls.

### Copy rules

- One `menu-lead` line under a title, ≤ ~90 chars. Field labels ≤ 3 words. Button labels ≤ 3 words.
- Depth goes in `title=` tooltips (`runTip` for run options) or a `help-fold` — **no paragraphs of body text** on functional screens. Game Info and Patch Notes are the prose/library screens (Info stays skimmable; Notes paginate by version).
- Hero card blurbs clamp to 1 line in compact grids.

### Motion & buttons

- Shared hover: **`shine-btn`** (shine sweep + `.btn-label` nudge), implemented once in `style.css` — never re-copy `::before` rules per widget.
- `shine-btn` goes on: primary/secondary menu CTAs, selectable hero cards, Randomize.
- `shine-btn` **never** goes on: gameplay HUD, `.tiny` tools, `.danger`/destructive (Quit, Delete, Reset, Stop), `:disabled`, icon-only controls (CSS also guards these).
- Reduce motion: Settings `reduceMotion` → `syncMotionPreference()` toggles `html.reduce-motion`; also honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. Kills shine, brand idle, aurora/waves; `mainMenuFx` takes `reduceMotion`.
- Menu music starts on the first user gesture (autoplay-block retry lives in `systems/music.ts` — window-level `pointerup`/`click`/`keydown` capture re-arm). Don't regress this to requiring a submenu visit.

### Anti-patterns (auto-model failure modes — reject on sight)

- A single centered column of stacked buttons/cards with dead space either side.
- Walls of explanatory text instead of tooltips/folds.
- Padding/font tweaks presented as a "redesign" while structure stays 1-column.
- Per-screen bespoke styles duplicating what a shared component already does.
- Native light-theme controls (`window.confirm`, unstyled selects/checkboxes).
- Fixed overlays appended outside the shell that survive re-renders.
- "Fitting" a screen by adding a scrollbar instead of restructuring.

### What not to do

- Don't restyle the in-match HUD with menu shine/hover chrome.
- Don't invent a second CSS framework or React layer for menus.
- Don't "improve" layouts by emptying the palette or switching fonts away from Orbitron / Rajdhani on brand surfaces.
- Don't expand every submenu into a novel one-off layout — extend tokens and shared classes first.

## Do / don't

- **Do** extend data + the system that already applies that kind of effect.
- **Do** keep Artifact shop entries separate from gear icon pipelines.
- **Do** update `PATCHNOTES.md` (+ **one** version bump per uncommitted batch — see Version + patch notes above), and this rule / `README.md` when conventions or advertised features change.
- **Don't** casually add new combat resources, currencies, or net message kinds without matching SP/MP and existing sync patterns.
- **Don't** fork a second game loop for desktop or single-file builds.
- **Don't** reintroduce shared-lane economy gating, client-side draft mutation in MP, or host-forced `viewTeam`.
